{
 "id": "1ch-6-priests",
 "title": "The High Priests",
 "ref": "1 Chronicles 6:1–15",
 "compact": true,
 "col": "japheth",
 "intro": [
  "The line of the high priests from Aaron to Jehozadak, who went into exile in 586 BC. His son Joshua (Jeshua) returned with Zerubbabel and served as high priest of the Second Temple (Haggai 1:1; Zechariah 3).",
  "The list is selective. It leaves out the line of Ithamar (Eli and his descendants), and some names repeat (Amariah, Ahitub, Zadok, Azariah), as was common in priestly families."
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah (Hebrew 5:27–41). Josephus, Antiquities 10.152–153; Babylonian Talmud, Yoma 9a. Parallel: Ezra 7:1–5.",
